  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OECD Anti-Corruption,Anti-bribery,IFF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to GovNet/Anti-Corruption Task Team PWB Budget and work plan 2021-2022 (and after that the next PWB) covering work related to anti-corruption and illicit financial flows. The Norwegian funding will be used for studies and research, dialogue  and meetings with stakeholders in order to collect new knowledge and best practice, for the  development of global and accetable principles, guidelines and approaches to solutions within the various working areas supported with particular relevance for developing countries,

The activities naims to foster accountable, inclusive and effective institutions, model integrity in development co-operation, and better identify and address the underlining linkages between IFFs and development. In the PWB 2021-2022 biennium, the ACTT has committed to (i) support the OECD-DAC in the fulfilment of its obligations to monitor and report on the implementation and continued relevance of the OECD Council Recommendation for Development Co-operation Actors on Managing the Risks of Corruption, and (ii) further recent efforts to develop a substantial body of work on IFFs and development.</narrative>
  </description>
